Reading a scroll of punishment by a wizard may be serious trouble if you
forget your offensive spell.

For any character, forgetting which scroll is "identify" spells serious
trouble: my current 17th level character lost that knowledge to a mind
flayer recently, and since he had already killed all shopkeepers,
price-ID was out of the question as well, so he had to resort to trying
out scrolls or waiting for a spellbook of identify (which he probably
couldn't have used anyway as a dumb barbarian). He decided to try out
scrolls, and got a scroll of amnesia as his reward.

So even knowing Identify in some form wouldn't be enough protection to
start reading blessed scrolls. I stick to my original advice: don't read
unknown scrolls (even if blessed)!

